              <p>Hi everyone,</p>
<p>In case you missed it, we’d like to remind everyone that <strong>starting on November 20</strong>, we will begin <a href="https://devforum.roblox.com/t/studio-beta-for-experience-controls-available-now/2567355">testing the updated experience controls</a> to a portion of users. The experience control layouts we are testing are all left-aligned, and some vary by the prominence of the text chat controls.</p>
<div align="center">
<p><img src="/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/c/5/9/c/c59c00bf4a1913a4f21040c5743db3a14994c7dd.gif" alt="image2" data-base62-sha1="sc8inkbjXxYyXeFputEfBj6mFlj" width="174" height="375" class="animated"></p>
<p><img src="/secure-uploads/uploads/original/5X/2/a/7/8/2a7836088e0f762060194bcfd6f88e431e07ea93.gif" alt="image1" data-base62-sha1="63HBuN2ivY8FIRSDEtO28pJOdpN" width="517" height="244" class="animated"></p>
</div>
<h3>
<a name="how-does-this-affect-me-1" class="anchor" href="#how-does-this-affect-me-1"></a>How does this affect me?</h3>
<p>If you have yet to make a design change to your UI, we encourage you to use the <a href="https://create.roblox.com/docs/en-us/reference/engine/classes/GuiService#TopbarInset">signal API </a>and/or the new <a href="https://create.roblox.com/docs/en-us/reference/engine/classes/ScreenGui#ScreenInsets">TopbarSafeInsets </a>API that are available across Roblox client and Studio to avoid collisions with your ScreenGui content. These APIs will make it easier for you to design your experience UI in a way that is compatible with the Roblox reserved space.</p>
<p>For FAQs and more details, please see our original DevForum post <a href="https://devforum.roblox.com/t/studio-beta-for-experience-controls-available-now/2567355">here</a>.</p>
            </div>

